{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-20T19:37:09.180Z","data":{"text":"Task 1 is complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n## Implementation\n\n**New `src/core/harness-catalog.ts`** — one frozen catalog of the four harnesses (`agy`, `opencode`, `mock`, `codex`) exposing:\n- normalized case-insensitive `lookupHarness`/`findHarness` and ordered `availableHarnessNames`\n- per-entry executable, model, effort resolution\n- planner-agent capability (agent support, default agent, native brief fallback)\n- `resolveExecutorIdentity` (selected harness only, `default` sentinel, effort or null, no cross-harness fallback)\n- `resolvePlannerSelection` (explicit planner wins; otherwise selected executor's entry; no model/effort/agent leakage)\n- re-homed 032 resolvers (`resolveCodex*`, `resolveHarness*`, `resolveAdapterModel`) so `src/core` has no harness-name branches and still never imports `src/harness`\n\n**Config modules**: `config-codex.ts` now derives planner validation (supported names, agent support) from the catalog and normalizes casing; `config.ts` applies `OSQ_MODEL` through catalog entries instead of per-harness comparisons; `config-doctor.ts` resolves binaries via catalog metadata.\n\n**`src/harness/index.ts`**: factory map typed `Record<HarnessName, () => HarnessAdapter>` for compile-time exhaustiveness, exported with runtime key parity, and `getHarnessAdapter` reports catalog names.\n\n**`src/index.ts`**: re-exports catalog helpers/types plus `validatePlannerConfig`.\n\n**New tests**: `tests/harness-catalog.test.ts` and `tests/config-planner-catalog.test.ts` cover every acceptance line.\n\n## Verification\n- Task verify: 27/27 pass.\n- `pnpm verify` (change-level): exit 0.\n- Full recursive suite: 750/754 pass. The 4 failures (`golden-events`, `delta-merge` ownership) are pre-existing 032 working-tree failures — they measure scaffolded content and living-spec globs, neither of which this task touches. Recorded in `.run/results/1.md` without editing frozen tests."}}
